00:02:34,800 --> 00:02:38,800
But I really do think they can be very impactful, okay?

39
00:02:38,800 --> 00:02:43,800
So, clickjacking is one of the things that you can do with iframes that's impactful to hacking.

40
00:02:43,800 --> 00:02:46,800
The other one is frame references, okay?

41
00:02:46,800 --> 00:02:53,800
So, frame references are extremely important when it comes to exploiting lots of client-side types of vulnerabilities.

42
00:02:53,800 --> 00:02:59,800
The reason for that is that if you have a reference to a frame, you can send a post message to it.

43
00:02:59,800 --> 00:03:05,800
If you're same origin, you can sort of jump into that page and grab the DOM and manipulate it and that sort of thing.

44
00:03:05,800 --> 00:03:19,800
So, especially in this era of like same site lacks default cookies, having a frame reference to a top-level page or something like that really allows you to manipulate that page a lot.

45
00:03:19,800 --> 00:03:24,800
But the most common, you know, use for having a frame reference is to send a post message, okay?

46
00:03:24,800 --> 00:03:25,800
What is a post message?

47
00:03:25,800 --> 00:03:30,800
A post message is inter-tab communication or inter-frame communication for the browser.

48
00:03:30,800 --> 00:03:40,800
And I really think that this is still, after me talking about it for years and years and years, a underserved attack surface, right?

49
00:03:40,800 --> 00:03:44,800
Like a lot of people just don't even look at post messages at all.

50
00:03:44,800 --> 00:03:50,800
And they're just completely missing an API that lives in the browser that is extremely important to the browser security, okay?

51
00:03:50,800 --> 00:03:52,800
So, definitely something to look into.

52
00:03:52,800 --> 00:03:57,800
I'll talk more about post messages maybe on a different like deep dive, technical deep dive episode like this.

53
00:03:57,800 --> 00:04:05,800
But for now, what you need to know is that iframe is one of the, the, the, okay, there's like a decent amount of ways to get a frame reference.

54
00:04:05,800 --> 00:04:08,800
But one of the few ways to get a frame reference is, is, is via iframe.

55
00:04:08,800 --> 00:04:09,800
Okay.

